Two programs store two million prices, 16 MB. Each function call gets a fixed slice of memory for its locals; here that slice is 8 MB.

```cpp
// A
int main() {
    double prices[2000000];
    prices[1999999] = 101.0;
}

// B
int main() {
    std::vector<double> prices(2000000);
    prices[1999999] = 101.0;
}
```

Each call gets a **frame** holding its locals and parameters. Step through the program.

```cpp
double mid(double bid, double ask) {
    return (bid + ask) / 2;
}
double value(int qty, double bid, double ask) {
    double m = mid(bid, ask);
    return qty * m;
}
int main() {
    double v = value(300, 99.5, 100.5);
    std::cout << v << "\n";
}
```

The pile of frames is the **stack**. `new` puts an object on the **heap** instead, where it stays until you `delete` it.

```cpp
double* make_price() {
    double* p = new double(101.5);
    return p;
}

int main() {
    double* q = make_price();
    std::cout << *q << "\n";
    delete q;
}
```

A **leak** is a `new` with no `delete`: the memory stays taken until the program ends. LeakSanitizer, part of `-fsanitize=address`, reports it at exit.

```cpp
double sum_prices(int n) {
    double* prices = new double[n];
    double total = 0;
    for (int i = 0; i < n; ++i) {
        prices[i] = 100 + i;
        total += prices[i];
    }
    return total;
}
```

A colleague frees an array of prices. In this browser the program runs, prints nothing odd, and exits with status 0.

```cpp
double* px = new double[1000];
// ... fill and use px ...
delete px;
```

widget.prelude:
#include <cstdio>
#include <cstdlib>
#include <iostream>
#include <new>
// A small leak checker: counts blocks from new[] and complains at exit if any never reached delete[]
namespace zq_heap {
long open_blocks = 0;
struct Check {
    ~Check() {
        if (open_blocks != 0) {
            std::cout.flush();
            std::fflush(stdout);
            std::fprintf(stderr, "leak check: %ld block(s) from new[] never reached delete[]\n", open_blocks);
            std::_Exit(1);
        }
    }
} check;
}
void* operator new[](std::size_t n) { ++zq_heap::open_blocks; void* p = std::malloc(n ? n : 1); if (!p) std::abort(); return p; }
void operator delete[](void* p) noexcept { if (p) --zq_heap::open_blocks; std::free(p); }
void operator delete[](void* p, std::size_t) noexcept { if (p) --zq_heap::open_blocks; std::free(p); }

