screens.prose:
The lifetimes you saw:

```cpp
void f(int n) {
    double x = 1.0;              // stack: dies at }
    double* p = new double(2.0); // heap: lives until delete
    double* a = new double[n];   // heap array: delete[]
    std::vector<double> v(n);    // v on the stack, its data on the heap
    delete p;
    delete[] a;                  // exactly once each
}
```

The stack is small, a few MB, and each call's frame takes some of it.

